<!--
    The Today's Pulse app shortcut's icon. MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT 13.5, design-v3.md 12.4.

    The Material Symbols Rounded `graphic_eq` glyph, weight 500, which is the same
    drawable `ic_graphic_eq.xml` ships and the same name design-v3.md section 7 maps this
    meaning to. Apache License 2.0.

    **It carries its own ground rather than borrowing the launcher's.** A shortcut icon
    is drawn by the launcher into a popup whose background follows the phone's theme,
    and it is not tinted, so a bare ink glyph is invisible in one of the two themes.
    The disc is the app icon's own #141A2E with the mark's #F3F1EC on it, so the row of
    three reads as this app in either theme and matches the icon they hang from.

    The glyph sits in the same 72 of 108 units `ic_launcher_foreground.xml` insets the
    mark to: the source viewport is 960 wide, 72/960 is the 0.075 scale below, and 18 is
    half of what is left. Nothing about it is a stripe, a bar or an edge, per CLAUDE.md
    rule 10.
-->
